Since the array $A$ is sorted, any subarray $A[L \dots R]$ is also sorted.
Intuitively, to maximize the number of pairs, we should try to pair the smallest available elements with the largest available elements that satisfy the condition. Why? Because smaller elements are easier to satisfy the condition $x \le y/2$ (since they are smaller), and larger elements are harder to satisfy the condition (since $y$ needs to be at least $2x$). Wait, actually, let's rephrase.
